{"path":"numeric/complex/log","title":"std::log(std::complex)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>log<small>(std::complex)</small>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/complex/log","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes complex natural (base e) logarithm of a complex value z with a branch cut along the negative real axis.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> log<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes complex <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_logarithm\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">natural (base <i>e</i>) logarithm</a> of a complex value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> with a branch cut along the negative real axis.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> complex value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, the complex natural logarithm of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is returned, in the range of a strip in the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−iπ, +iπ]</span> along the imaginary axis and mathematically unbounded along the real axis.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Error_handling_and_special_values\">Error handling and special values</h3>\n<p>Errors are reported consistent with <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/math_errhandling\">math_errhandling</a></span>.\n</p><p>If the implementation supports IEEE floating-point arithmetic,\n</p>\n<ul><li> The function is continuous onto the branch cut taking into account the sign of imaginary part\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw1332\">std::<span class=\"me2\">log</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conj</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conj</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw1332\">std::<span class=\"me2\">log</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(-0,+0)</code>, the result is <code>(-∞,π)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_DIVBYZERO</a></span> is raised\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+0,+0)</code>, the result is <code>(-∞,+0)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_DIVBYZERO</a></span> is raised\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(x,+∞)</code> (for any finite x), the result is <code>(+∞,π/2)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(x,NaN)</code> (for any finite x), the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(-∞,y)</code> (for any finite positive y), the result is <code>(+∞,π)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,y)</code> (for any finite positive y), the result is <code>(+∞,+0)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(-∞,+∞)</code>, the result is <code>(+∞,3π/4)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,+∞)</code>, the result is <code>(+∞,π/4)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(±∞,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(+∞,NaN)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,y)</code> (for any finite y), the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,+∞)</code>, the result is <code>(+∞,NaN)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code>\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The natural logarithm of a complex number <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> with polar coordinate components <span class=\"texhtml\">(r,θ)</span> equals <span class=\"texhtml\">ln r + i(θ+2nπ)</span>, with the principal value <span class=\"texhtml\">ln r + iθ</span>.\n</p><p>The semantics of this function are intended to be consistent with the C function <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/clog\"><code>clog</code></a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// r = 1, θ = pi / 2</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"2 * log\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw1332\">std::<span class=\"me2\">log</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z2 <span class=\"br0\">{</span>sqrt<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, sqrt<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// r = 1, θ = pi / 4</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"4 * log\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu16\">4.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw1332\">std::<span class=\"me2\">log</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z3 <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// r = 1, θ = pi</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"log\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z3 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw1332\">std::<span class=\"me2\">log</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z3<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z4 <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// the other side of the cut</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"log\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z4 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (the other side of the cut) = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw1332\">std::<span class=\"me2\">log</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z4<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>2 * log(0,1) = (0,3.14159)\n4 * log(0.707107,0.707107) = (0,3.14159)\nlog(-1,0) = (0,3.14159)\nlog(-1,-0) (the other side of the cut) = (0,-3.14159)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2597\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2597</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>specification mishandles signed zero imaginary parts\n</td>\n<td>erroneous requirement removed\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/log10\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>log10<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  complex common logarithm with the branch cuts along the negative real axis <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/exp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>exp<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  complex base <i>e</i> exponential <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>log</span><span>logf</span><span>logl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes natural (base <span class=\"texhtml\">e</span>) logarithm (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\ln{x}}\">ln(x)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/log\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>log<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\">std::log</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/clog\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>clog</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Error handling and special values","id":"Error_handling_and_special_values"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::log(std::complex)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Computes complex natural (base e) logarithm of a complex value z with a branch cut along the negative real axis."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, the complex natural logarithm of z is returned, in the range of a strip in the interval [−iπ, +iπ] along the imaginary axis and…"},{"label":"Error handling and special values","note":"Errors are reported consistent with math_errhandling."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The natural logarithm of a complex number z with polar coordinate components (r,θ) equals ln r + i(θ+2nπ), with the principal value ln r + iθ."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"log10(std::complex)","note":"complex common logarithm with the branch cuts along the negative real axis"},{"label":"exp(std::complex)","note":"complex base e exponential"},{"label":"log, logf, logl","note":"computes natural (base e) logarithm (ln(x))"},{"label":"log(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::log to each element of valarray"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":525,"codeBlockCount":2}
